{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123241","id":4454100092,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCXwsfA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123241","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123241.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123241.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123241","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123241/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123241/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123241/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e1080e78df278ebdb06fcfe531947571993185a0","number":123241,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add iterators and range-for support to `SelfList`","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nThis adds `Iterator`, `ConstIterator`, `begin` and `end` to `SelfList` and replaces all applicable loops in the codebase with range-for loops, hopefully resulting in less visual noise and more maintainable code.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThere's currently quite a lot of this kind of thing going on in parts of the codebase that use `SelfList`:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nfor (SelfList<SomeThing> *some_element = some_list.first(); some_element != nullptr; some_element = some_element->next()) {\r\n    some_element->self()->bar();\r\n    some_element->self()->baz();\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAs well as the `while`-loop equivalent:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nSelfList<SomeThing> *some_element = some_list.first();\r\nwhile (some_element != nullptr) {\r\n    some_element->self()->bar();\r\n    some_element->self()->baz();\r\n    some_element = some_element->next();\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nWe've obviously largely left this kind of iteration behind with all the other collections, but `SelfList` has remained for some reason, so this PR aims to modernize it with proper iterators and range-for support:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nfor (SomeThing& some_element : some_list) {\r\n    some_element.bar();\r\n    some_element.baz();\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote however that this PR deliberately does not convert code that uses this kind of pattern:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nfor (SelfList<SomeThing> *some_element = some_list.first(); some_element != nullptr;) {\r\n    SelfList<SomeThing> *next_element = some_thing->next(); // Get the next element right away, since we won't be able to after the removal.\r\n    some_list.remove(&some_element); // Can also be `some_element->remove_from_list()`\r\n    some_element = next_element;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n... since removing an element clears its next/prev pointers, which would stop a range-for loop in its tracks.\r\n\r\nThe iterators here are copied pretty much verbatim from `List<T>`.\r\n\r\nMost of the changes here have not been explicitly tested, since the changes were very mechanical, but what few MRPs and demo projects I tested still run just fine.","labels":[{"id